eq\mathsf{PP} [CGG+23]. On the other hand, there are barriers to showing that the existence of EFI implies any conjectures in complexity theory [LMW24]. In this work, we will characterize one-way puzzles with the average-case hardness of estimating Kolmogorov complexity. Our results will naturally generalize the characterizations of [IRS21], corroborating the centrality of one-way puzzles in quantum cryptography, and providing the first complexity-theoretic characterization of a quantum cryptographic primitive. Furthermore, we will argue that this is in some sense the only possible characterization of one-way puzzles based on the hardness of a meta-complexity problem.

